story=intro('KAELEB HECK / MR. BLINDBANDIT','BLIND ARTIST.<br><span>BOUNDLESS</span><br>IMAGINATION.','Recording artist. Producer. Digital storyteller. Founder of Blindbandit Records.')
story+='''<section class="shell story-layout"><div class="sticky-photo"><img src="/assets/artist.jpg" alt="Kaeleb Heck, known as Mr. Blindbandit" width="531" height="640" loading="lazy"><p class="eyebrow">Virginia roots / Philippines home</p></div><div class="story-copy"><p class="large-copy">A creative world built through sound.</p><p>Mr. Blindbandit is Kaeleb Heck, an American recording artist, producer, and content creator with roots in Virginia and a home in the Philippines. His work brings music, video, and personal storytelling together under one independent creative identity.</p><h2>THE ARTIST</h2><p>Blind since birth, Kaeleb creates with screen readers and accessible technology. His identity as a blind creator is part of the perspective he shares, alongside the everyday work of writing, producing, releasing, and connecting with listeners.</p><p>His music moves across ambient, cinematic, electronic, dreamcore, hip-hop, and experimental sounds. This range gives listeners more than one entry point: immersive soundscapes, beat-driven releases, collaborations, and alternate versions that revisit an idea from another angle.</p><h2>THE MUSIC</h2><p>The catalog stretches from singles such as Sapphire castles and Genesis to projects including The eternal bloom, Time flies, Flying high, weightless, and cry forever. EPs, albums, and individual tracks sit beside extended and dreamscape versions.</p><p>That variety is a defining part of the Mr. Blindbandit world. The music page brings these releases together so listeners can trace the catalog across years, explore a full project, or start with a single track.</p><h2>THE INDEPENDENT SPIRIT</h2><p>As the founder of Blindbandit Records, Kaeleb connects the roles of artist, producer, and independent creator. The label is part of a wider creative practice that includes Mr. BlindBandit Studios, video, and digital storytelling.</p><p>Collaboration is part of that world too. Shared releases connect Mr. Blindbandit with UUu Tang Maskman, Yxngfery, Pablo Jackson Hairston, and other credited artists. Each connection offers another way into the music—and another artist for listeners to discover.</p><h2>LIFE BEYOND THE STUDIO</h2><p>With Virginia roots and a home in the Philippines, Kaeleb’s public channels extend beyond music releases. He shares everyday life, creative work, and his perspective as a blind creator with an audience that can follow the person as well as the artist.</p><p>Accessibility is part of how that work happens. Screen readers and accessible technology support the creative process, while his public storytelling gives space to a perspective that is often missing from conversations about music and digital creation.</p><p>Follow the official channels for the ongoing story, explore the catalog for the sound, or get in touch to discuss a creative connection.</p><a class="button" href="/connect/">Connect with Mr. Blindbandit ↗</a></div></section>'''+ticker()
story+='<section class="shell section">'+heading('Blindbandit Records','BLIND-OWNED.<br>CREATOR-DRIVEN.')+'<div class="portal-grid"><div><span>01 / SOUND</span><h3>Independent music</h3><p>Music across genres, formats, and creative directions.</p></div><div><span>02 / PERSPECTIVE</span><h3>Accessible creation</h3><p>A creative practice supported by screen readers and accessible technology.</p></div><div><span>03 / CONNECTION</span><h3>Shared imagination</h3><p>Collaborators, listeners, and stories that cross borders.</p></div></div></section>'
layout('/story/','The story','Meet Kaeleb Heck, the artist and producer behind Mr. Blindbandit and Blindbandit Records.',story)

